    board(review): file CF-171 — CF-002's allowlist claim has no in-repo artifact
    
    The review lane picked 3c78dd1 ("board: CF-002 model allowlist + revocation
    proven") as the week's largest claim against its evidence. The commit asserts
    that a proxy refuses any model outside CF_PROXY_ALLOWED_MODELS, re-reads the
    token file per request, and that six live probes returned 200/403/400/401/401/
    200 — while its diff is two board lines.
    
    Measured at origin/main 20f93ad (fresh clone, parity 0 0):
      git ls-tree -r HEAD --name-only | grep -ci inference          -> 0
      grep -rn CF_PROXY_ALLOWED_MODELS .                            -> no hits
      git merge-base --is-ancestor 114cc2c HEAD                      -> rc 1
      grep -c CF-002 specs/HARNESS.md docs/THREAT-MODEL.md docs/OPERATIONS.md -> 0 0 0
    
    So AC1 ("a test proves every other model/route is refused") cannot be re-run
    from the published repo, and AC5 ("blast radius stated in specs/HARNESS.md")
    is unmet, while docs/ACCEPTANCE-PLAN.md 205-220 cites 3c78dd1 as superseding
    the "a node turn cannot start inference" blocker. The behaviour is real but
    lives outside the tree: ~/.hermes/scripts/cf-inference-proxy.py (186 lines,
    listening on 0.0.0.0:8775), with the in-repo implementation plus its 764-line
    contract test stranded on non-ancestor 114cc2c (origin/wt/CF-002-0937).
    
    Filed CF-171 with three re-runnable criteria; the repair is future work and is
    not claimed here.
    
    Gates at this tree: bash tests/selftest.sh -> SELFTEST: PASS (rc 0, 106 PASS
    rows); bash scripts/boardctl validate -> RESULT: OK (3 pre-existing warnings).
    gh run list -> [] (the repo ships no workflows).
    
    Transport: this tick's candidate root (/home/kara/code-factory) carried four
    sibling code-factory lanes running from the same 02:18:14 spawn, so the row
    was written in a fresh clone of origin/main (remote gh added explicitly) and
    the candidate root was left untouched. A fresh clone carries no installed
    pre-commit hook, so the GitReins guard is evidenced by the explicit
    `gitreins task complete CF-171-RV1` run, not by a commit hook.
    
