 {"id":"CF-168","title":"P3 — tests/selftest.sh 7b can report a FALSE red under set -uo pipefail: printf | grep -q answers 141 on SIGPIPE after the text matched, so a passing arm grades FAIL","status":"pending","priority":"P3","complexity":3,"created_at":"2026-11-04T06:56:27Z","updated_at":"2026-11-04T06:56:27Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"5d4b380b6158d0f2054bf856b0c0923886b50a4781244c44d66af2400c74798d"},"reasoning":"Observed once while gating 5fc2cbd in this lane's tick (code-factory-duckbrain-releng-2026-11-04-06-11-13): a full `bash tests/selftest.sh` run graded section 7b's `number` arm FAIL — `FAIL  number fixture escaped the board gate (exit 1)` — while the same arm printed `FAIL  board line 2: expected JSON object, got 42` and `FAIL  2 of 3 rows parse` and exited 1, i.e. every condition the arm asserts was satisfied. Two further runs at the same tree answered `SELFTEST: PASS` / 106 rows, and 20 isolated iterations of the same fixture never reproduced it, so the arm itself is not broken: the ASSERTION is.\n\nMechanism: tests/selftest.sh:3 sets `set -uo pipefail`; the arm's conditions at tests/selftest.sh:242-244 are `printf '%s\\n' \"$out\" | grep -Fq ...` / `grep -Fxq ...` / `! ... | grep -q ...`. `grep -q` exits as soon as it matches, so `printf` can take SIGPIPE on its remaining write; `pipefail` then makes the pipeline answer 141 even though grep matched, the `&&` chain falls through to the else branch, and the suite prints a false FAIL and increments `fails`. Deterministic demonstration (the row's probe): a writer that prints the match first and then more lines yields `assert_rc=141` on three consecutive runs.\n\nWhy it matters: this is the inverse of the suite's own doctrine (\"a green that cannot go red is decoration\") — a red that cannot be trusted is just as useless, and a single flaky arm makes a whole tick's gate evidence ambiguous: a releng/review lane cannot distinguish a real regression from a 141, and the tidiest response (re-run until green) is 